(:id "port/python/packet/ranged-integers" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/python/kind_int.go" "internal/codegen/python/python_packet_ranged_bits_test.go: TestPythonPacketRangedBits, TestPythonPacketRangedBitsNegativeControl, TestPythonPacketRangedBitsGoReferenceNegativeControl" "make/python-packet-ranged-bits.mk: python-packet-ranged-bits-negative-control, python-packet-ranged-bits-goref-negative-control" "make generated-current") :tested-revision "95f76165fe9cd27bb7edc136499f915336eba9d2" :note "2026-11-15: the test's own fixture (ranged integers alone, beside bits(N), and beside the core's bool, bare int32 and a nested type) writes the same bytes as the generated Go code and reads the Go bytes back to the same value under both pins, every declared default included; it covers each range's minimum and maximum, an interior value, the int32 and int64 ranged paths, the full-range uint64 path and a degenerate range. Every below-minimum, above-maximum and non-int write raises InvalidValue, and an offset above the span, a truncated input and a trailing byte refuse. bench_ints, whose kinds are only the core's and these, reads and writes back byte-identical. The Go reference control moves one range minimum in a copy of the generated module and goes red on its marker. Run on Linux x86_64 with the pinned CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2 (make dist-python), SCHEMA_SLOW=1, and make generated-current, at this revision.")
(:id "port/python/packet/bits" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/python/kind_bits.go" "internal/codegen/python/python_packet_ranged_bits_test.go: TestPythonPacketRangedBits, TestPythonPacketRangedBitsNegativeControl, TestPythonPacketRangedBitsGoReferenceNegativeControl" "make/python-packet-ranged-bits.mk: python-packet-ranged-bits-negative-control, python-packet-ranged-bits-goref-negative-control" "make generated-current") :tested-revision "95f76165fe9cd27bb7edc136499f915336eba9d2" :note "2026-11-15: the test's own fixture writes bits(N) at widths 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 9, 33 and 64, alone, beside ranged integers and beside the core's kinds, byte-identical to the generated Go code, and reads the Go bytes back to the same value under both pins, declared defaults included. Out-of-range and non-int writes raise InvalidValue, and truncated input, a trailing byte and nonzero padding refuse. probebits and bench_bits, whose kinds are only the core's and these, read and write back byte-identical. The negative control rewrites a copy of the generated ProbeBits reader and goes red on the write-back marker. Run on Linux x86_64 with the pinned CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2 (make dist-python), SCHEMA_SLOW=1, and make generated-current, at this revision.")
